  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a chlorosulfamoyl salicylanilide (xipamide-like) scaffold; among the supplied contexts it is closest to metolazone, whose absolute oral bioavailability is ~100% (C15), with L2 estimates of 65% and 60–80% (C22, C26), all far above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C15","C22","C26"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sulfonamide-containing comparators in the supplied records consistently exceed 20%: valdecoxib 83% (C01/C02/C05/C12; L2 C20/C21), meloxicam 91% (C03), pritelivir 75% (C16), ixazomib 58–60% (C06/C07/C14/C17), and PF-05241328 38% (C04/C10/C25).",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C10","C12","C14","C16","C17","C20","C21","C25"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Celecoxib's 20–40% value is explicitly attributed to poor aqueous solubility (C09); the query's ionizable, lower-logD profile is not the same solubility-limited case, and 20–40% is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C09"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The new L3 oral exposure records (C30–C41) show measurable oral AUC/Cmax for indapamide, lumiracoxib, and N-Ac-5-ASA, but none include an IV comparator or absolute F; they are therefore neutral for the F >= 20% threshold and do not alter the prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-molecule-specific oral bioavailability record is present; the prediction relies on structural analogy and class-consistent high-F records.",
    "The L3 oral AUC/Cmax records lack IV comparators or absolute F estimates and are for other molecules.",
    "No query-specific formulation, dose, prandial state, or first-pass/clearance data are supplied.",
    "The physicochemical prior is mixed (low neutral fraction, high TPSA) and cannot by itself confirm permeability, but it does not affirmatively support F < 20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) for the query's chlorosulfamoyl salicylanilide (xipamide-like) scaffold, based on close analogy to metolazone (L1 ~100%; L2 65% and 60–80%) and consistent high absolute oral bioavailability of sulfonamide-containing comparators (valdecoxib 83%, meloxicam 91%, pritelivir 75%, ixazomib 58–60%, PF-05241328 38%). The only low-F sulfonamide record (celecoxib 20–40%) is solubility-limited and not transferable. New L3 oral AUC/Cmax records are exposure-only and neutral; confidence remains moderate."
}

